Description: composefs-backed remote snapshotter for containerd
 cfs-snapshotter is a containerd remote (proxy) snapshotter that serves
 container root filesystems from a content-addressed, composefs-backed
 store: a container mounts its image's read-only EROFS metadata once,
 shared by all its containers, and gets one flat overlay whose data comes
 from fs-verity-protected objects.
 .
 By default a plain docker/containerd pull fills the store; started with
 -admit=preloaded the daemon instead serves only images placed
 in the store out of band with ocicfs, pinned by digest. Building pulled
 images into the store uses mkcomposefs from the composefs package.
